        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132-a16">

                <pb facs="0234" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg154"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Miller.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Russian minister says he will telegraph consul that Russian authority only
                    replaces Chinese, and that all treaty rights must be respected and all former
                    lawful practices followed, and direct him to meet you and try amicably to settle
                    all questions. You can hardly claim complete and exclusive jurisdiction of
                    Chinese subjects because they live in American houses.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
